+
+## Native input capacity evaluation (not released)
+
+The evaluation branch separates source-horizon arrays and depths (`mxhzin=11`)
+from calculation-layer arrays (`mxnsl=10`). Counts outside 1–11 stop explicitly.
+All existing aggregation operations, the 1800 mm clamp and final-horizon extension
+remain unchanged. Shared calculation depths are populated only by the existing
+calculation-grid loop. No runtime output or pass dimension is expanded.
+
+`tests/test_native_soil_input_capacity.py` compiles the actual reader and its
+native dependencies with bounds checks, then inspects calculation state for
+multiple OFEs, format variants, capacity boundaries and equivalent subdivisions.
+`tools/evaluate_soil_input_capacity.py` compares full three-year runs using
+baseline/candidate binaries and retained source inputs. This prototype does not
+relax WEPPpy's production ten-horizon contract or authorize a release.
